question:
For a Binomial distribution with 5 trials and $P = \frac{1}{4}$, find the probability that:
(i) Exactly 3 trials are successful;
(ii) At least 2 trials are successful;
(iii) Less than 4 trials are successful;
(iv) All the 5 trials are successful;
(v) None of the trials is successful.

If a card is randomly selected from a deck of cards, find the probability that it is:
(i) A spade or a diamond;
(ii) An ace or a heart.
